  "title": "what a visible group's rectangle is made of",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "group-boxes Q1 — the boundary's geometry",
  "explanation": "Two ways to draw a group's boundary, each with what it costs below it. [The derived side](#derived-side) gets half the no-ambiguity requirement for nothing and pays when a member is dragged far away; [the own-rectangle side](#own-rectangle-side) keeps a stable box and pays by letting the member list and the drawing disagree. It leaves out how either one is enforced during a drag, which is the next question.",
